WEBVTT

00:00.775 --> 00:04.538
This is Neuron. I won't tell you how it works, but I can show you what it does.

00:04.588 --> 00:06.112
Every point is a word.

00:06.162 --> 00:09.350
Every line is a relationship it formed on its own.

00:10.984 --> 00:14.309
I'll start with a word it has never been given.

00:15.193 --> 00:17.293
The line I typed is the primary run.

00:17.343 --> 00:21.268
Underneath it, the engine spawns its own secondary runs, one for every

00:21.318 --> 00:23.106
thing it had to understand on the way.

00:23.156 --> 00:24.793
Those are the counts.

00:25.702 --> 00:27.552
Now a different word.

00:28.469 --> 00:29.706
Look at the last row.

00:29.756 --> 00:33.257
Every question has a shape, and the first time it meets a new one it works

00:33.307 --> 00:37.819
out a formula. Here the formula was already there, so it used it again.

00:38.694 --> 00:40.819
A meaning isn't fixed.

00:42.319 --> 00:46.169
I can tell it, in one line, that a word means something else, and the relationships

00:46.219 --> 00:49.106
move with it. No retraining, no rebuild.

00:49.156 --> 00:51.769
Just a change of state, with a time on it.

00:52.703 --> 00:55.466
Ask for the word again and it answers from memory.

00:55.516 --> 00:58.478
The run it did is still there, as a receipt.

00:59.678 --> 01:00.828
So let's play it back.

01:00.878 --> 01:03.228
This is the path through the graph, hop by hop.

01:03.278 --> 01:06.666
Every hop is readable, which means every answer can be audited.

01:06.716 --> 01:08.353
Learning happens at build time.

01:08.403 --> 01:10.628
This is runtime, and it's quick.

01:12.012 --> 01:17.412
That's Neuron. Research and engineering by James Huson, at exnulla dot com.
